{"case_id":"C051","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":100,"affected_functions":["fuzz/c/std/gif_fuzzer.c:fuzz","fuzz/c/std/zlib_fuzzer.c:fuzz"],"reason":"S1 changes wuffs_base__status from int32_t to a struct containing code, but H0 still treats returned statuses as scalar integers and passes them directly to status-string functions that now accept int32_t. Thus S1 + H0 is API-incompatible and cannot adequately exercise the decoder entry points, while these operations were valid under S0.","evidence":["S1 replaces `typedef int32_t wuffs_base__status` with `typedef struct { int32_t code; } wuffs_base__status`.","Both harnesses use `if (z)`, which assumes `wuffs_base__status` is scalar.","gif_fuzzer.c calls `wuffs_gif__status__string(z)` and compares `z == WUFFS_BASE__SUSPENSION_END_OF_DATA`, while S1 declares `wuffs_gif__status__string(int32_t status_code)` and status constants remain integer codes.","zlib_fuzzer.c compares `z != WUFFS_BASE__SUSPENSION_SHORT_WRITE` and calls `wuffs_zlib__status__string(z)`, while S1 declares `wuffs_zlib__status__string(int32_t status_code)`.","The production implementation itself demonstrates the required S1 protocol through checks such as `status.code`, construction via `WUFFS_BASE__MAKE_STATUS`, and calls to status-string functions with integer status codes."],"recommended_action":"Update both harnesses to inspect status through `z.code` or the `wuffs_base__status__is_*` helpers, compare `z.code` with integer status constants, and pass `z.code` to `wuffs_gif__status__string` and `wuffs_zlib__status__string`."}
